WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.691
Match the accelerator to the memory and compute profile of the job.

00:00:04.691 --> 00:00:08.900
VRAM must hold model weights, context cache, activations, runtime overhead, and,

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.961
for training or fine-tuning, optimizer and gradient state.

00:00:11.961 --> 00:00:15.404
Model file size alone is not a complete requirement.

00:00:15.404 --> 00:00:17.700
Longer context, larger batches, vision inputs,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.291
and concurrent sequences can raise memory use after the model has loaded.

00:00:22.291 --> 00:00:26.117
GPU generation affects supported numerical formats, software compatibility, and performance.

00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:31.091
Memory bandwidth influences how quickly large model weights can be moved during inference.

00:00:31.091 --> 00:00:34.917
Raw compute matters more for some training and image workloads.

00:00:34.917 --> 00:00:39.509
Review measurements from a comparable model and runtime rather than assuming that

00:00:39.509 --> 00:00:42.570
a higher product number is always more economical.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.161
A single high-memory GPU is often easier to use than several smaller

00:00:47.161 --> 00:00:50.604
devices when one model must fit as a unit.

00:00:50.604 --> 00:00:55.196
Multi-GPU instances can support model parallelism, larger training jobs, or multiple replicas,

00:00:55.196 --> 00:00:59.787
but the framework must distribute work effectively and interconnect performance can matter.

00:00:59.787 --> 00:01:03.613
Several GPUs do not automatically create one shared memory pool.

00:01:03.613 --> 00:01:07.439
Inference usually prioritizes memory fit, latency, throughput, and serving efficiency.

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:10.883
Fine-tuning may require much more memory and checkpoint storage.

00:01:10.883 --> 00:01:14.326
Quantization can make inference practical on a smaller rental,

00:01:14.326 --> 00:01:17.004
while parameter-efficient tuning can reduce training requirements.

00:01:17.004 --> 00:01:20.448
Vision and multimodal models add image-processing and memory demands.

00:01:20.448 --> 00:01:24.657
Test the smallest plausible configuration with real prompts, context, and batches,

00:01:24.657 --> 00:01:28.100
then move upward only when measurements identify a constraint.
